clausis-core (0.5.0-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Remove the automatable D-Bus phrase/PIN approval transport.
  * Capture the random phrase and voice PIN only inside the isolated trusted
    confirmation service and submit its capability directly to ActionBroker.
  * Canonicalize public-bus provenance and reject caller-supplied capabilities.
  * Add spoken or masked PIN enrollment and private Calamares verifier copy.
  * Require the pinned local speech runtime for trusted confirmation.
  * Add local wake, activation-timeout, sleep and emergency-stop gating before
    any Hermes or cloud fallback.
  * Add a bounded AT-SPI GNOME adapter for orientation, numbered controls,
    semantic back navigation and accessible window cycling.
  * Add deterministic repeat, correction and cancellation voice commands.
  * Keep all hardware in honest half-duplex until a local interruption
    detector and physical Barge-in tests exist.
  * Add a matching accessible Clausis GNOME identity and GDM branding.
  * Document the remaining audio, GNOME, installer, confirmation and recovery
    work required before claiming complete voice-only operation.
  * Preinstall pinned Hermes Agent 0.20.0 in the live and target system.
  * Add accessible GTK, Orca, keyboard and local-voice provider setup.
  * Carry staged Hermes settings into the Calamares target account privately.
  * Install the latest official stable Hermes release during installation,
    retaining the pinned image version as an offline and failure fallback.
  * Add voluntary OpenAI Realtime speech with separate consent, private key
    storage, typed broker actions, local stop and automatic offline fallback.
  * Bind the exact selected disk and destructive profile immediately before
    Calamares writes partitions and require a protected spoken random phrase.
  * Generate, speak and enroll a high-entropy LUKS2 recovery key without
    exposing key material through process arguments or Calamares state.
  * Derive ISO names and release assets from one authoritative project version.

 -- Clausis contributors <maintainers@example.invalid>  Fri, 07 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0200
